From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: report 802.11be in the build feature query
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Answer "hostapd -v11be" with success when the package is built with
CONFIG_IEEE80211BE. The Wi-Fi 7 overlay carries an older copy of
build_features.h that knows 11ac and 11ax only. LuCI asks this question
before it offers a mode, so it dropped BE from the Mode list and showed an
empty field for a radio configured for BE.

Port of the build_features.h hunk of OpenWrt commit
b1d6068330c7c23be6d0d2a5c3e8a72ac6e25ac1 ("hostapd: add
CONFIG_DRIVER_11BE_SUPPORT", Janusz Dziedzic). Nothing in the wireless
start scripts asks this question, so radio bring-up is unchanged.

diff --git a/feeds/qca-wifi-7/hostapd/src/src/utils/build_features.h b/feeds/qca-wifi-7/hostapd/src/src/utils/build_features.h
index 553769ec..cc883153 100644
--- a/feeds/qca-wifi-7/hostapd/src/src/utils/build_features.h
+++ b/feeds/qca-wifi-7/hostapd/src/src/utils/build_features.h
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@ static inline int has_feature(const char *feat)
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "11ax"))
 		return 1;
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "11be"))
+		return 1;
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211R
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "11r"))
 		return 1;
